> Preserve the original fourteen-vertex instance

The native fixture retains the original xorshift seed12345, edge-presence modulo
two and integer weights one through nine. It has fourteen vertices and fifty
undirected edges. The exact helper fixes vertex zero to one side, enumerating
8192 complement classes instead of both orientations of every partition. All
objective sums here are small exact integers, so the exhaustive comparison has
no floating ambiguity.

One hundred actual restarts with alpha0.3 and seed1 replace the old repeated
calls for budgets1 through40. Their summaries contain the producing local result
and best-so-far value. The figure uses the first forty summaries from this
single run. Monotonic best-so-far retention is guaranteed; a rising curve or a
hit on the optimum is not guaranteed for every instance or seed. A flat curve
may mean the first restart already found the optimum.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/grasp_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto adj = dm::algorithms::grasp_demo_graph();
    const auto exact = dm::algorithms::grasp_exact_max_cut(adj);
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::grasp_max_cut_trace(14, adj, 100, .3, 1);
    std::size_t entries = 0;
    for (const auto &row : adj)
        entries += row.size();
    std::print("Original vertices {}; undirected edges {}; GRASP best {}; exhaustive best {}; examined " "complement classes {}.\n\n",
               adj.size(), entries / 2, t.run.result.value, exact.result.value,
               exact.partitions);
    std::print("| restart | local final value | actual prefix best | improved retained best |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 40; ++i) {
        const auto &r = t.restarts[i];
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        y.push_back(r.best_value);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, r.final_value,
                   r.best_value, r.improved_best);
        if (i && y[i] < y[i - 1])
            throw std::runtime_error("best prefix");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual prefix best", {5, 150, 105}, 2).points(x, y, "",
                                                                {5, 150, 105}, 4).abline_h(exact.result.value, {220, 38, 38}, 1.5).title("Original graph: actual one-run restart prefixes").x_label("completed restarts").y_label("best cut weight").y_limits(170, 195).save_svg("build/grasp_original.svg");
    if (exact.result.value != 186 || t.run.result.value != 186 ||
        entries / 2 != 50)
        throw std::runtime_error("original fixture");
}
